# bend-rig: forming leads in the bending rig (decision C19, the user's
# design): arm A slides the resistor's lead 2 into the rig, 3 mm from
# the body at the mandrel; the clamp and anvil close on it from opposite
# sides and the former bends it down round the mandrel; the arm puts the
# bent leg through the rig's shear, which trims it to 8 mm; then the
# resistor is soldered to the chip by its straight lead 1, as in solder.
reset circuit=demo
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=0,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.2 at=3
scope aim=R1.2 zoom=3
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.2 at=8
lift A mm=60
move A to=0,60,60 rpy=180,0,90
move A to=34.81,1.27,-14.05
align A R1.1.tip to=U1.3.tip gap=0.1
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=6
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+R1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
unpinch P1
